## Configuration Options

### Binary Paths

- `helm_binary_path` - Specify a custom path to the Helm binary. If not set, the provider searches for `helm` in the system PATH.
- `kustomize_binary_path` - Specify a custom path to the Kustomize binary. If not set, the provider searches for `kustomize` in the system PATH.

### Initialization

- `perform_init` - When set to `true`, the provider runs `helmfile init` before applying any operations. This ensures that all required Helm plugins and dependencies are installed.
- `skip_refresh` - When set to `true`, skips running `helmfile repos` before applying operations. This can speed up operations if repositories are already up to date.

### Repository Management

- `disable_force_update` - When set to `true`, prevents forced updates of Helm repositories when executing `helm repo add`.
- `skip_deps` - When set to `true`, skips running `helm repo update` and `helm dependency build`.

### Plugin Management

- `additional_plugins` - List of additional Helm plugins to install. Each entry should be a URL or plugin identifier.
- `enforce_plugin_verification` - When set to `true`, enforces verification of Helm plugins when installing missing ones.

### Security

- `strip_args_values_on_exit_error` - When set to `true` (default), strips potential secret values from Helm command arguments in error messages.
- `helm_oci_plain_http` - When set to `true`, allows using plain HTTP when pulling charts from OCI registries. **Use with caution in production.**

### Global Arguments

- `default_args` - List of arguments to pass to every Helmfile command. These are applied globally across all operations.

## Authentication

The provider uses the Kubernetes configuration from your environment. It respects:

- `KUBECONFIG` environment variable
- `~/.kube/config` file (default)
- In-cluster configuration (when running in a Kubernetes pod)

Individual resources can override the kubeconfig, context, and namespace settings.

## Plugin Requirements

The provider requires the following Helm plugins to be installed:

- [helm-diff](https://github.com/databus23/helm-diff) - For generating diffs between releases

These can be automatically installed by setting `perform_init = true` or by listing them in `additional_plugins`.
